WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.489 --> 00:00:03.793
- Don't judge yourself in the daily.

00:00:03.793 --> 00:00:05.848
Judge yourself in the yearly.

00:00:05.848 --> 00:00:08.869
And slow it down, be patient.

00:00:08.869 --> 00:00:09.955
Yeah!
- Yeah!

00:00:09.955 --> 00:00:12.263
- [Gary] You've got your perspective.

00:00:12.263 --> 00:00:15.023
- [Announcer] Gary Vaynerchuk!

00:00:15.023 --> 00:00:17.988
- [Gary] I just wanna be happy

00:00:17.988 --> 00:00:20.631
(reflective piano music)

00:00:20.631 --> 00:00:22.767
I enjoy paying my dues.

00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:26.627
I loved when I was 28, on December ninth,

00:00:26.627 --> 00:00:28.402
working a register,

00:00:28.402 --> 00:00:30.393
because it was busy in the store,

00:00:30.393 --> 00:00:33.886
and having my friends from
college come to the store

00:00:33.886 --> 00:00:36.612
in their BMW, 'cause they
worked on Wall Street,

00:00:36.612 --> 00:00:38.482
and they're buying a case of wine,

00:00:38.482 --> 00:00:40.943
and they're looking dead in my face

00:00:40.943 --> 00:00:42.325
and I know what they're thinking,

00:00:42.325 --> 00:00:44.124
which is, they just
pulled up into my store

00:00:44.124 --> 00:00:46.876
in their BMW and I'm the help,

00:00:46.876 --> 00:00:49.418
going downstairs to pick
up their case of champagne.

00:00:49.418 --> 00:00:51.334
I enjoyed those moments,

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:54.852
because I knew exactly
how it was gonna play out.

00:00:54.852 --> 00:00:57.269
- [Female] I love you, Gary!

00:01:01.187 --> 00:01:02.561
- For me, happiness is

00:01:02.561 --> 00:01:06.346
being able to do what you
want to do at all times.

00:01:06.346 --> 00:01:08.041
- [Interviewer] Not
conforming or pandering.

00:01:08.041 --> 00:01:10.305
- Just being able to
do what you want to do!

00:01:10.305 --> 00:01:11.138
I mean, that's

00:01:11.138 --> 00:01:11.971
(audio distorts)

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:13.029
who wouldn't what that?

00:01:13.029 --> 00:01:14.388
And I think that is one of the

00:01:14.388 --> 00:01:16.745
great things about entrepreneurship.

00:01:16.745 --> 00:01:18.851
The cost of that is,

00:01:18.851 --> 00:01:21.533
you're always one second away from dying.

00:01:21.533 --> 00:01:22.366
Right?

00:01:22.366 --> 00:01:23.611
Entrepreneurship is scary!

00:01:23.611 --> 00:01:24.714
One second you're at the top of the world,

00:01:24.714 --> 00:01:26.549
next, there is nobody behind you.

00:01:26.549 --> 00:01:28.093
You're the last line.

00:01:28.093 --> 00:01:28.926
It's like fighting a war.

00:01:28.926 --> 00:01:29.939
Just you, you're the last.

00:01:29.939 --> 00:01:30.772
This is the castle.

00:01:30.772 --> 00:01:31.605
You.

00:01:31.605 --> 00:01:32.702
Everybody's been fighting, you.

00:01:32.702 --> 00:01:34.583
So that's lonely, that's scary.

00:01:34.583 --> 00:01:36.672
But, you get to define it.

00:01:36.672 --> 00:01:38.031
You get to tell what everybody's

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:39.203
where they positioned and

00:01:39.203 --> 00:01:40.036
how they should

00:01:40.036 --> 00:01:41.514
and so, I love that feeling.

00:01:41.514 --> 00:01:44.536
I love being in that place.

00:01:44.536 --> 00:01:46.096
Loving what you do is so

00:01:46.096 --> 00:01:47.893
people hear that,

00:01:47.893 --> 00:01:48.772
even when I was a kid,

00:01:48.772 --> 00:01:49.735
I was like, ah that's bull

00:01:49.735 --> 00:01:51.500
it's very fluffy,

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:53.474
but it's very true!

00:01:53.474 --> 00:01:55.308
Being happy in what you do?

00:01:55.308 --> 00:01:56.899
And whether that's making $45,000 a year

00:01:56.899 --> 00:01:59.074
or $4,000,000 a year,

00:01:59.074 --> 00:02:00.738
if you really love it,

00:02:00.738 --> 00:02:01.993
and you're really doing
what you wanna be doing,

00:02:01.993 --> 00:02:03.766
that's a very, very good place to be,

00:02:03.766 --> 00:02:04.985
you're just going to be happy.

00:02:04.985 --> 00:02:07.191
And I genuinely do think we have

00:02:07.191 --> 00:02:10.616
a major branding issue on success.

00:02:10.616 --> 00:02:13.287
And I mean across 7.7 billion people.

00:02:13.287 --> 00:02:14.912
Every part of the world.

00:02:14.912 --> 00:02:16.828
And I'm very passionate about

00:02:16.828 --> 00:02:19.916
being one of the voices
that tries to redefine it.

00:02:19.916 --> 00:02:22.540
Because I'm unbelievably
not driven by money.

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:23.898
Unbelievably.

00:02:23.898 --> 00:02:25.024
I spent the first 12 years of my life

00:02:25.024 --> 00:02:26.406
building a family business

00:02:26.406 --> 00:02:28.298
from a 3 to a $60,000,000
business for my parents

00:02:28.298 --> 00:02:30.852
and left at 34 years old
with nothing to my name.

00:02:30.852 --> 00:02:32.164
Then started a company with my brother

00:02:32.164 --> 00:02:33.685
who was coming out of college,

00:02:33.685 --> 00:02:35.496
and made him a 50-50 partner,

00:02:35.496 --> 00:02:36.530
and then he left four years later

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:39.270
and I spent tens of millions
of dollars to buy him out.

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:41.580
Money does not drive me.

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:43.124
The game.

00:02:43.124 --> 00:02:46.457
(modern pop rock music)

00:02:56.783 --> 00:02:59.797
I'm unbelievably in
tune with the fact that

00:02:59.797 --> 00:03:02.165
it's almost impossible
to become a human being,

00:03:02.165 --> 00:03:03.210
and I have no interest

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:05.172
for taking that for granted.

00:03:05.172 --> 00:03:08.481
(reflective piano music)

00:03:08.481 --> 00:03:10.846
I love when analytical people,

00:03:10.846 --> 00:03:13.888
when I have a very deeply
math kid in front of me

00:03:13.888 --> 00:03:15.211
and we're having some sort of debate,

00:03:15.211 --> 00:03:16.105
and they're upset about something,

00:03:16.105 --> 00:03:18.044
I'm like, you do know the
odds of being a human being

00:03:18.044 --> 00:03:20.627
are 400 trillion to one, right?

00:03:22.227 --> 00:03:24.449
I think that what drives me is

00:03:24.449 --> 00:03:27.143
an unbelievably clear perspective

00:03:27.143 --> 00:03:30.556
to how lucky we are to have an at bat.

00:03:30.556 --> 00:03:33.900
And I'm struggling to dwell on dumb shit.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:36.535
As long as eight people
that I love more than life

00:03:36.535 --> 00:03:38.439
are alive that morning,

00:03:38.439 --> 00:03:39.902
I'm in good spirits.

00:03:39.902 --> 00:03:41.388
I really am.

00:03:41.388 --> 00:03:42.221
Yeah.

00:03:42.221 --> 00:03:43.304
You know?

00:03:43.304 --> 00:03:45.579
I think adversity and humble beginnings

00:03:45.579 --> 00:03:47.848
is an incredibly good
framework to happiness

00:03:47.848 --> 00:03:50.167
if you layer positivity and optimism

00:03:50.167 --> 00:03:52.675
around your difficulty.

00:03:52.675 --> 00:03:54.149
A lot of times people
look at their difficulty

00:03:54.149 --> 00:03:56.239
and dwell and go the other way.

00:03:56.239 --> 00:03:57.072
So for me,

00:04:00.868 --> 00:04:02.044
I'm excited every day,

00:04:02.044 --> 00:04:03.832
'cause I get to play.

00:04:03.832 --> 00:04:06.816
And yes, I love competing, but

00:04:06.816 --> 00:04:09.614
I love competing more than,

00:04:09.614 --> 00:04:13.166
I love the game more than the
trophy that the game gives me.

00:04:13.166 --> 00:04:15.628
And that is also another happy part.

00:04:15.628 --> 00:04:18.077
But I have my perspective
in check, I really do.

00:04:18.077 --> 00:04:19.738
And I don't just say it, I live it.

00:04:19.738 --> 00:04:22.396
And what's really fun for me is that,

00:04:22.396 --> 00:04:23.348
I'm a little bit older,

00:04:23.348 --> 00:04:24.266
when this has all happened,

00:04:24.266 --> 00:04:25.601
so I have a lot of people in my life

00:04:25.601 --> 00:04:26.959
who've known me long before I ever made

00:04:26.959 --> 00:04:28.422
one single piece of
content on the internet

00:04:28.422 --> 00:04:29.255
in the wine world,

00:04:29.255 --> 00:04:31.464
let alone what it's manifested into.

00:04:31.464 --> 00:04:32.297
And it's funny,

00:04:32.297 --> 00:04:33.263
when once in a blue moon

00:04:33.263 --> 00:04:34.459
if some things fester

00:04:34.459 --> 00:04:37.594
and there's a little bit
of pushback against me,

00:04:37.594 --> 00:04:38.557
it's really fun to see

00:04:38.557 --> 00:04:41.890
grammar school and high school and college

00:04:41.890 --> 00:04:43.445
and early wine people jump in and be like,

00:04:43.445 --> 00:04:45.268
this is gonna be fuckin',

00:04:45.268 --> 00:04:46.917
you think this is somebody else,

00:04:46.917 --> 00:04:49.564
this is who this dude was
when nobody was watching.

00:04:49.564 --> 00:04:50.397
You know?

00:04:50.397 --> 00:04:51.584
I've always been very grateful.

00:04:51.584 --> 00:04:52.652
I'm very grateful.

00:04:52.652 --> 00:04:54.498
I'm very grateful.

00:04:54.498 --> 00:04:58.265
(reflective piano music)

00:04:58.265 --> 00:05:01.376
You should always be doing what you want.

00:05:01.376 --> 00:05:03.292
- [Female] Even if nobody responds to it

00:05:03.292 --> 00:05:05.042
- You don't know yet.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.005
Not at first.

00:05:08.005 --> 00:05:10.165
To your point, if you do
something for a year and a half

00:05:10.165 --> 00:05:12.835
and nobody gives a fuck,
now you're delusional.

00:05:12.835 --> 00:05:16.504
But, but notice that
I'm giving you an answer

00:05:16.504 --> 00:05:18.512
based on where you're at now.

00:05:18.512 --> 00:05:20.045
If you don't have a podcast yet,

00:05:20.045 --> 00:05:22.518
you should start with what you love.

00:05:22.518 --> 00:05:25.269
Because the only way you're
gonna do something hard enough

00:05:25.269 --> 00:05:26.895
is if you love it.

00:05:26.895 --> 00:05:27.789
You know?

00:05:27.789 --> 00:05:29.658
So you start with something you love,

00:05:29.658 --> 00:05:33.187
you do it for a year, you feel it out,

00:05:33.187 --> 00:05:34.952
and if you're now into year two

00:05:34.952 --> 00:05:36.148
and nobody still is,

00:05:36.148 --> 00:05:37.692
now it's, people always

00:05:37.692 --> 00:05:39.875
the hardest question to ask is

00:05:39.875 --> 00:05:41.512
when should you double down on

00:05:41.512 --> 00:05:43.207
staying the course and persevering,

00:05:43.207 --> 00:05:44.937
or when should you bail and shut it down?

00:05:44.937 --> 00:05:46.086
You never really,

00:05:46.086 --> 00:05:47.375
I can never answer that question.

00:05:47.375 --> 00:05:48.501
There's too much I need to know

00:05:48.501 --> 00:05:49.836
to answer that question.

00:05:49.836 --> 00:05:51.044
But in the beginning point,

00:05:51.044 --> 00:05:52.553
it's very easy for me to answer.

00:05:52.553 --> 00:05:54.260
Do something you fuckin' love

00:05:54.260 --> 00:05:56.895
because if you're doing
something you think will do well,

00:05:56.895 --> 00:05:58.079
you're now already in a place

00:05:58.079 --> 00:06:00.761
where it's gonna be hard
for you to make the content.

00:06:00.761 --> 00:06:01.597
I'm passionate about it,

00:06:01.597 --> 00:06:02.700
you have so much other shit.

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:05.185
You're gonna choose what
else is better or easier,

00:06:05.185 --> 00:06:06.018
you know?

00:06:06.018 --> 00:06:07.460
It's hard to get going

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:08.853
around something you
don't feel great about,

00:06:08.853 --> 00:06:10.014
you're just doing it for what?

00:06:10.014 --> 00:06:10.850
For the listens?

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:12.267
For the subscribes?

00:06:12.267 --> 00:06:13.100
For what?

00:06:14.055 --> 00:06:16.214
I'm so passionately trying to get people

00:06:16.214 --> 00:06:19.381
to realize happy is better than money.

00:06:20.452 --> 00:06:22.321
I'm passionate about this.

00:06:22.321 --> 00:06:24.596
I'm passionate about this.

00:06:24.596 --> 00:06:26.257
It's a very important conversation,

00:06:26.257 --> 00:06:27.174
we have to.

00:06:28.242 --> 00:06:31.133
If we wanna really really
really change shit,

00:06:31.133 --> 00:06:34.755
we have to redefine
what success looks like.

00:06:34.755 --> 00:06:37.263
It is just not how many
subscribers you have,

00:06:37.263 --> 00:06:38.630
it is not how much money you make.

00:06:38.630 --> 00:06:40.522
It's just not.

00:06:40.522 --> 00:06:43.262
And people are pandering to the machines,

00:06:43.262 --> 00:06:44.551
the algorithms, the subscriptions,

00:06:44.551 --> 00:06:45.468
and ultimately, why?

00:06:45.468 --> 00:06:46.722
For the money.

00:06:46.722 --> 00:06:47.555
Right?

00:06:47.555 --> 00:06:48.893
You're gonna pander for the subscriptions

00:06:48.893 --> 00:06:49.726
and for the likes,

00:06:49.726 --> 00:06:50.797
'cause that leads to the brand deals,

00:06:50.797 --> 00:06:52.004
the money and this is something that

00:06:52.004 --> 00:06:54.686
I think we need to talk about.

00:06:54.686 --> 00:06:57.705
It's something, we're now
mature enough in this ecosystem

00:06:57.705 --> 00:06:58.738
that it's time for us to now have

00:06:58.738 --> 00:07:00.688
more thoughtful conversations.

00:07:00.688 --> 00:07:03.208
We have to start having this conversation.

00:07:03.208 --> 00:07:06.916
(light hip hop influenced pop music)

00:07:06.916 --> 00:07:08.240
- I know it's all about what you do

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:10.172
after full time work, but

00:07:10.172 --> 00:07:11.298
do you feel like

00:07:11.298 --> 00:07:12.421
is that too much?

00:07:12.421 --> 00:07:13.338
(audio distorts)

00:07:13.338 --> 00:07:16.031
Balance between creating content

00:07:16.031 --> 00:07:20.443
- Are you able to afford
not doing your job?

00:07:20.443 --> 00:07:22.649
- Because my side business

00:07:22.649 --> 00:07:24.182
- Varied.
- And my content

00:07:24.182 --> 00:07:26.849
- Can you control your expenses?

00:07:27.887 --> 00:07:29.019
- I can.

00:07:29.019 --> 00:07:31.701
- I mean, that's, it's
a very practical answer.

00:07:31.701 --> 00:07:33.118
I get that one would want to

00:07:33.118 --> 00:07:36.740
you gotta nail down, it is after your job.

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:39.213
Obviously you'd love to
not have to do your job.

00:07:39.213 --> 00:07:40.873
You only got two options.

00:07:40.873 --> 00:07:43.590
Wait 'til your side hustles get to enough

00:07:43.590 --> 00:07:45.053
that you can leave your job,

00:07:45.053 --> 00:07:48.768
or, leave your job and
live way more humbly

00:07:48.768 --> 00:07:50.428
with roommates or back home

00:07:50.428 --> 00:07:51.705
or whatever the hell it is.

00:07:51.705 --> 00:07:52.538
- Yeah.

00:07:52.538 --> 00:07:54.469
- Those are the only two real options.

00:07:54.469 --> 00:07:57.139
- So you won't suggest doing
three at the same time.

00:07:57.139 --> 00:07:59.345
- I think three at the same time is fine.

00:07:59.345 --> 00:08:00.796
I don't think you're stretched too thin

00:08:00.796 --> 00:08:03.002
or doing too many things.

00:08:03.002 --> 00:08:04.465
I think that that's great,

00:08:04.465 --> 00:08:05.544
if you can maintain it,

00:08:05.544 --> 00:08:06.868
as long as you don't mentally burn out.

00:08:06.868 --> 00:08:08.401
- Burn out, yeah.
- Yeah.

00:08:08.401 --> 00:08:09.387
And even if, by the way,

00:08:09.387 --> 00:08:12.801
do three things, burn out, and drop one!

00:08:12.801 --> 00:08:14.159
- Drop one.
- You know what I mean?

00:08:14.159 --> 00:08:16.040
What works today doesn't have to be

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:17.201
what works tomorrow.

00:08:17.201 --> 00:08:18.118
- Right.

00:08:18.118 --> 00:08:20.521
- This is one big game of self awareness.

00:08:20.521 --> 00:08:22.913
It's not how I want it,
it's not how you want it.

00:08:22.913 --> 00:08:24.689
It's how you need it for yourself.

00:08:24.689 --> 00:08:26.373
You just need to keep asking yourself,

00:08:26.373 --> 00:08:27.206
what do you need?

00:08:27.206 --> 00:08:28.474
And what you need today

00:08:28.474 --> 00:08:29.960
is different than what
you're gonna need tomorrow,

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:31.922
and it's different than
what you needed yesterday.

00:08:31.922 --> 00:08:34.035
This is a forever evolving thing.

00:08:34.035 --> 00:08:37.588
Evolve to what feels right today,

00:08:37.588 --> 00:08:40.688
not what you think it should be.

00:08:40.688 --> 00:08:41.698
- Great stuff, Gary.

00:08:41.698 --> 00:08:42.531
Thank you.

00:08:42.531 --> 00:08:44.020
- Happy to do it.

00:08:44.020 --> 00:08:45.053
- So Gary, if there's one thing

00:08:45.053 --> 00:08:46.493
you want to tell every creative out there

00:08:46.493 --> 00:08:48.176
that's struggling now that's trying to

00:08:48.176 --> 00:08:49.012
get up to their career,

00:08:49.012 --> 00:08:51.090
what would that one thing be?

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:53.529
- It takes years of great creative work

00:08:53.529 --> 00:08:54.573
to get to that place.

00:08:54.573 --> 00:08:55.955
Stop judging yourself.

00:08:55.955 --> 00:08:58.486
Just 'cause this one video
didn't get as many views

00:08:58.486 --> 00:09:00.274
or not as many likes,

00:09:00.274 --> 00:09:02.608
don't judge yourself in the daily.

00:09:02.608 --> 00:09:04.465
Judge yourself in the yearly,

00:09:04.465 --> 00:09:06.160
and slow it down.

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:06.993
Be patient.

00:09:06.993 --> 00:09:07.844
- Be patient.

00:09:07.844 --> 00:09:09.411
I love that, thank you so so much.

00:09:09.411 --> 00:09:11.584
(inaudible)

00:09:11.584 --> 00:09:14.767
- How do you deal with this sadness?

00:09:14.767 --> 00:09:16.671
Just once in your life?

00:09:16.671 --> 00:09:17.577
One time?

00:09:17.577 --> 00:09:19.191
- I mean, I struggled when I was a kid

00:09:19.191 --> 00:09:21.757
because I hated school.

00:09:21.757 --> 00:09:23.312
But since I've been a grown up,

00:09:23.312 --> 00:09:24.880
not so much.

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:26.447
Not really, and I'll tell you why.

00:09:26.447 --> 00:09:27.852
Any time I start getting sad,

00:09:27.852 --> 00:09:29.512
I get sad like anybody else,

00:09:29.512 --> 00:09:31.741
I immediately put things in perspective.

00:09:31.741 --> 00:09:32.833
- [Female] Put things in perspective.

00:09:32.833 --> 00:09:34.773
- And here's what I do.

00:09:34.773 --> 00:09:36.208
Context.

00:09:36.208 --> 00:09:38.146
Just 'cause this business thing,

00:09:38.146 --> 00:09:42.995
or just because these people
said this thing about me,

00:09:42.995 --> 00:09:44.900
what would happen if my mom died today?

00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:45.782
- Bye, Gary!

00:09:45.782 --> 00:09:47.152
- To the women out there
- Bye, guys.

00:09:47.152 --> 00:09:49.281
- The women out there,
what are you gonna say?

